---
---

<section id="how" class="section" data-track-section="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Describe the agent. Point it at a project. Read the log.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You write what should happen in two Markdown and YAML files. Duskfleet runs it and writes
        down what happened.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step panel">
        <span class="step__n">01</span>
        <h3 class="step__title">Write an agent.</h3>
        <p class="step__text">
          A Markdown file with YAML frontmatter: model, permission mode, allowed tools, budget. Or
          link an agent your project already defines.
        </p>
        <pre class="code"><code>---
id: test-fixer
model: sonnet
permission_mode: acceptEdits
allowed_tools: [Bash(npm test:*)]
max_budget_usd: 1
---
Fix failing tests. Never skip one.</code></pre>
      </li>

      <li class="step panel">
        <span class="step__n">02</span>
        <h3 class="step__title">Launch from chat, CLI or cron.</h3>
        <p class="step__text">
          Ask Claude Desktop over MCP, type a command, or set a 5-field cron. A busy agent is
          skipped, never queued.
        </p>
        <pre class="code"><code><span class="dim">$</span> duskfleet run \
    --project app --agent test-fixer \
    --model haiku -- "Fix the failing test"

<span class="dim">#</span> or, in Claude Desktop:
<span class="mid">"run test-fixer on app every night at 2"</span></code></pre>
      </li>

      <li class="step panel">
        <span class="step__n">03</span>
        <h3 class="step__title">Read what happened.</h3>
        <p class="step__text">
          Every event lands in SQLite and a JSONL log. The dashboard shows the timeline, the result,
          the cost, and resumes the session with one command.
        </p>
        <div class="code log">
          <div class="log__row"><span class="dim">00:00</span><span>Read package.json</span></div>
          <div class="log__row"><span class="dim">00:04</span><span>Bash npm test</span></div>
          <div class="log__row"><span class="dim">00:41</span><span>Edit src/cron.ts</span></div>
          <div class="log__row"><span class="dim">01:02</span><span class="log__amber">Bash git push · denied</span></div>
          <div class="log__row"><span class="dim">01:03</span><span class="log__ok">result · $0.11 · 6 turns</span></div>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .intro {
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 40px 0 0;
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .step__n {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 19.5px;
    color: var(--sunset-amber);
  }

  .step__title {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 33px;
  }

  .step__text {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 22.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .step .code {
    margin-top: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .log {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 7.5px;
    padding: 12px 14px 13px;
    line-height: 19px;
  }

  .log__row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .log__row .dim {
    width: 52px;
    flex: none;
  }

  .log__amber {
    color: var(--sunset-amber);
  }

  .log__ok {
    color: var(--ok);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      max-width: 560px;
    }
  }
</style>
